# The app's runtime data directory. Umbrel rsyncs this tree into `app-data` at install (dropping
# the .gitkeep files), which is how the bind-mount source exists and is owned by the right uid
# before the container first starts — Docker would otherwise create it as root.
#
# The DIRECTORIES are tracked, through their .gitkeep files. Nothing else under here ever may be:
# on a machine that has actually run the app, `archives/` holds encrypted copies of every
# customer's quotes and `secrets/` holds the production database password. This repository is
# public.
tenon-joinr-backup/data/**
!tenon-joinr-backup/data/**/
!tenon-joinr-backup/data/**/.gitkeep

# The same rule for Joinr Finance, whose data directory on a machine that runs it holds the
# owner's finance database and every backup of it, and for Joinr Registry, whose data directory
# holds the stored images. Directories and their .gitkeep files only.
tenon-joinr-finance/data/**
!tenon-joinr-finance/data/**/
!tenon-joinr-finance/data/**/.gitkeep
tenon-joinr-registry/data/**
!tenon-joinr-registry/data/**/
!tenon-joinr-registry/data/**/.gitkeep
